<section class="solution-diagnostic section fade-up">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-title center">
<span>START WITH THE SYMPTOM</span>
<h2>Where Is Your Program Losing Margin?</h2>
<p>Most expensive failures begin as a small mismatch between requirement, interface and operating reality. Choose the signal that looks familiar.</p>
</div>
<div class="diagnostic-grid">
<a href="/solutions/energy-storage-systems.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>ENERGY & GRID</span><h3>The plant meets nameplate, but still curtails, trips or misses dispatch.</h3><p>Look at grid strength, PCS limits, EMS/BMS ownership, protection timing and site commissioning evidence.</p><b>Diagnose BESS & grid integration →</b></a>
<a href="/solutions/thermal-management.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>THERMAL</span><h3>The prototype passes, but production units run hot or derate early.</h3><p>Look at loss distribution, interface pressure, tolerance stack-up, coolant balance, airflow and aging.</p><b>Recover thermal margin →</b></a>
<a href="/solutions/semiconductor.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>HARDWARE & EMC</span><h3>The board works on the bench, then fails EMC, reliability or production ramp.</h3><p>Look at component derating, switching loops, return paths, parasitics, DFM and supplier variation.</p><b>Review components & PCBA →</b></a>
<a href="/solutions/automation.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>CONTROL & INTEGRATION</span><h3>Subsystems pass alone, but the integrated machine or vehicle behaves unpredictably.</h3><p>Look at timing, state ownership, degraded modes, interface contracts and end-to-end validation.</p><b>Close integration gaps →</b></a>
<a href="/solutions/robotics-motion-control.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>ROBOTICS & MOTION</span><h3>The robot moves in the lab, but payload, heat, falls and real duty cycles expose the joints.</h3><p>Look at actuator sizing, servo bandwidth, EtherCAT timing, battery transients, EMC, safety and reliability growth.</p><b>Engineer robot reliability →</b></a>
<a href="/solutions/industrial-networking.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>DATA & NETWORK</span><h3>Intermittent faults disappear before logs explain what happened.</h3><p>Look at clock alignment, traffic deadlines, observability, stale data and recovery behavior.</p><b>Build diagnosable connectivity →</b></a>
<a href="/solutions/engineering-consulting.html" class="diagnostic-card"><span>PROGRAM RISK</span><h3>Reviews are happening, but critical assumptions remain ownerless.</h3><p>Look at requirements quality, FMEA evidence, decision records, supplier boundaries and release criteria.</p><b>Structure the engineering decision →</b></a>
</div>
</div>
</section>

