</div>
</details>
{% endfor %}
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="solution-deliverables section fade-up">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-title center">
<span>WHAT THE ENGAGEMENT PRODUCES</span>
<h2>Engineering Evidence, Not Another Presentation</h2>
<p>Every engagement is scoped around a decision your team must make and the evidence required to make it safely.</p>
</div>
<div class="deliverable-grid">
<div class="deliverable-card"><b>01</b><h3>Problem & Boundary Definition</h3><p>Operating envelope, failure signature, interface ownership, assumptions and measurable acceptance criteria.</p><span>Output: engineering brief + evidence plan</span></div>
<div class="deliverable-card"><b>02</b><h3>Architecture & Design Review</h3><p>Cross-domain review of power, thermal, control, communications, safety, component and manufacturing risks.</p><span>Output: findings ranked by mechanism and impact</span></div>
<div class="deliverable-card"><b>03</b><h3>Technology & Supplier Decision</h3><p>Application-specific comparison covering margin, qualification, integration effort, supply continuity and lifecycle.</p><span>Output: decision matrix + qualification gaps</span></div>
<div class="deliverable-card"><b>04</b><h3>Validation & Root-Cause Plan</h3><p>Instrumentation, corner cases, fault injection, decision rules and traceability from requirement to evidence.</p><span>Output: executable DVP / investigation plan</span></div>
<div class="deliverable-card"><b>05</b><h3>Integration & Commissioning Support</h3><p>End-to-end state, timing and protection verification under nominal, transient and degraded conditions.</p><span>Output: issue closure + commissioning evidence</span></div>
<div class="deliverable-card"><b>06</b><h3>Production & Field Feedback Loop</h3><p>Supplier/process controls, traceability, telemetry and field-return learning fed back into the design baseline.</p><span>Output: control plan + corrective-action loop</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="engagement-path section fade-up">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-title center">
<span>HOW TO ENGAGE</span>
<h2>Start At The Point Of Highest Risk</h2>
<p>You do not need a fully written scope. Bring the symptom, requirement, failed test or decision that is blocking the program.</p>
</div>
<div class="engagement-steps">
<div><strong>01</strong><h3>Frame</h3><p>We identify the physical or process boundary and the decision that needs evidence.</p></div>
<div><strong>02</strong><h3>Interrogate</h3><p>We review data, design artifacts and assumptions across the interfaces where risk concentrates.</p></div>
<div><strong>03</strong><h3>Resolve</h3><p>We provide prioritized actions, owners, validation criteria and supplier or implementation support.</p></div>
<div><strong>04</strong><h3>Close</h3><p>We stay through verification so findings become released design or operating controls.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

